Z||000000||javier_altube||12-29-2001||06:10 PM||||hey, my name is Javier, and I'm about to buy an 86 SE, automatic, V 6,  2.8, with 89k<BR>i want to know if i've to know anything in particular about this car, i like the car, it looks clean, but I don't know if comes with any problem from factory<P>thanks for your help<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||avengador1||12-29-2001||06:18 PM||||You can use carfax to get some information on the car, otherwise you should check it over very carefully yourself. Make sure the body panels line up and don't have excessive gaps. Look underneath for dents and scrapes. Check under the carpeting in the trunk for rust. Look at the battery tray for rust. Have someone drive it and drive behind it to see how it tracks on the road. Drive it and check how it shifts and sounds. Pull the wheels off and look at the pads, rotors, shocks, and struts. Look for any leaks and their sources. Hope this helps. A lot of these cars have been taken good care of and should prove to be reliable, but beware of the ones that have been abused as they can prove to be quite expensive to repair/restore. Bye the way, welcome to the forum. Enjoy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg">   <P>[This message has been edited by avengador1 (edited 12-29-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by avengador1 (edited 12-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||javier_altube||12-29-2001||06:23 PM||||thanks avengador1, just to let you know, the car has been sit for like 5 years, and as i remember the last time that the car started was almost 2 years ago||||reg||10
